! Forks that await the operator's word

''Both forks the operator owed are RULED and LANDED (see #/landed): `:814` → Option 1 (`6b0910fbc`), ④ → keep-separate (`dacae83b8`). No open operator forks remain — only the deferred+pinned items in #/deferred and the small follow-ons in #/hazards.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/deferred>>

! Deferred + pinned — do not lose

# ''① `tend.repair` + the LAMPLIGHTER / KAHU cabal split'' — ''LAMPLIGHTER'' = independent operators who RUN + TEND INFRASTRUCTURE (herms, islands, relays); ''KAHU'' = stewards of the Nexus/DreamNet SOFTWARE + GRAMMAR (the memetic-wikitext grammar, the protocol — the TW5-Syntax arc is Kahu ground); some operators hold BOTH. ''Prerequisite (operator):'' a human watches a browser↔node session where file projections TEAR, before the caretaker's reach gets designed. ''Plan:'' (1) two has-cap STACKS composed not fused — Lamplighter (run/tend/repair/recover infra) + Kahu (grammar/software/protocol stewardship); (2) the FROST k-of-n threshold Place-DID cure for `tend.repair`→`@daemon` — a Lamplighter cap must not reach a herm's raw signing key alone; a quorum signs a repair, the herm's own `@daemon` testimony stays independent; (3) red-first: `tend.repair` cannot sign `@daemon` solo. RULING owed: the FROST split + the cap boundary. Deferred, PINNED.
# ''The self-slot INNER ring'' — NARROWS-only (can only tighten a self-verdict), bounded one-message-wide + an IRREVERSIBLE naming freeze (a bag URL through a live ring hashes to seed its Document; a re-name costs a re-founding). ''Plan:'' (1) widen the bridge first — a `bagUrlForDoc` resolver at the shore (reversible); (2) then, ONLY on an explicit operator ruling of the naming freeze, wire it. No admission-widening urgency pulls it forward. RULING owed: the naming freeze, deliberately.
# ''The ahi-kā deferred knobs'' — ''hard gate:'' a Negative-Binomial estimator fit against Elyncia's 500-year event corpus (calibrate the rate params, replacing the fiction-QA defaults). ''Then:'' (a) the hysteresis gap — revival cost scales with cold-depth (no thrash); (b) the commons-vs-hearth exemption — a private single-steward hearth never colds, a multi-steward commons cools normally. Red-first each. No ruling owed; gated purely on the estimator.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/crossroads-syntax>>

! The crossroads watch — the TW5-Syntax arc on `release/3.0.0`, live 2026-09-18

The grammar's own ground: the `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` submodule, where the founding hearth's sections above do not reach. Commit hashes name the submodule unless marked PARENT.

''Landed (condensed):''
* ''The opener namespace'' — `{{ << (( < <$ <%` share one tag family, a link's `[[` keeps its own, a call reads as a widget does; seven floors re-seated carrying their ruling (`32291b2`).
* ''The darkness witness'' — every line of every construct the host builds, judged MISS or LOST; 41 lines over 71 carriers declared OWED (`819d8e6`).
* ''Five instrument holes closed'' — the oracle's walk keeps what a pragma nests (`3680592`) · a delimiter claim answers to the tightest cover (`0ba7540`) · corpus overreach gated (`7266646`) · swallow-witness names the regions its probe cannot ask (`f70f1de`) · the bracket witness reads VS Code's unmatched red (`72318ac`). 566 tests, 47 gates.
* ''The corpus trued'' — the markdown host retired, `doctype` keyed on the declaration rather than the extension (PARENT `10061cc9d` · `3224409c3`).

''Merged onto `release/3.0.0` (2026-09-18):'' the zero-cost batch — thirteen red-first fixes and rulings (`9d3fbc3`); TOML 1.1 through the private `source.toml.tw5-syntax`, sublimehq's grammar hand-ported, `ini` on `source.ini`, the fence guarded (`3d39456`); the instruments — divergence-staleness over every overreach run, sibling-aware ruling matching, the ablation witness as a gate (`d037501`). 590 tests, 49 gates. Darkness 41 → 22, rulings 136 → 111. The comment-form DOCTYPE retired from the whole tree; six pre-ruling fixtures ride typed-ahu carriers (PARENT `4dd44e74d` · `6b1dd63a1`).

''Forward paths:''
# ''Look'' — the bench serves the merged tree; the operator's eyes-on pass, which decides the ship.
# ''The carrier truth pass'' — each carrier states what TiddlyWiki reads: `tables.spans` (a `b` suffix the host lacks, a row-opening `<`), `blocks.tables` labels, `pragmas.signatures` (a `((…))` default only a `\procedure` reads), the bare `\rules` in `tiddlywiki5.pragma.tw`, pragmas below content in `spans.multiline`; the new `tables.nesting` and `tables.malformed` carriers.
# ''Retire the owed ledgers'' — darkness (41), brackets (3), and the OWED rulings in `expected-divergence`: a list item after a closing html line, adjacent code runs, `<![CDATA[`, and the verdicts TiddlyWiki never passes (`ambiguous-ampersand`, the two `html.deprecated` verdicts).
# ''Stopped on their price, awaiting a ruling'' — one scheme spelling (two floors fall, one by 3; the in-link half alone costs 0) · italic and inline code across lines by a blank-line bound (overreach and the attribute ceiling fail) · tags across blank lines with quoted values yielding (swallow-witness unasked 18 → 52, still-reach below its floor, and the yielding value leaves the tag open over the heading).
# ''The ablation witness's neutral letter'' — a replacement letter can BUILD markup (`[imgx ]]` opens an image reading into the next line), so a MISS it reports needs tracing; the witness owes a test that discounts structure its own replacement creates.
# ''Rulings still owed'' — one ruling for italic AND inline code across lines; the tag blank-line bound; the MVV attribute's whitespace (the batch returns the trace); the name inside `((`.
# ''Instruments still owed'' — a stale check for `expected-divergence` (its rulings serve four runs, so idleness needs their union); the ablation witness for AST shape the tables spirit proposed.
# ''The reader-distinction ranking'' — write which distinctions a reader needs most, in order, before the next palette session.
# ''TOML 1.1 in full'' — a hand port of the sublimehq grammar, the only one covering it.
# ''Ship'' — on the operator's word: `release/3.0.0` → tag → cut on merge to `main`, then the parent's submodule pointer.

''Pinned — approved, enact on the next quiet window (a Sonnet spirit):''
* ''The tree-sitter four-backtick fence'' — `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext/grammar.js` `fenced_block` closes a fence at ANY triple-backtick line, so it reads inside a four-backtick fence that `fence-mask` holds as one block. Six held-text carriers and 73 `bags/` carriers that quote examples in four-backtick fences parse without error nodes yet lose the block. The cure: a fence closes only on a run at least as long as its opener (the rule `fence-mask` already keeps), red-first against a four-backtick specimen holding a triple-backtick line; then regenerate the committed `src/parser.c` with the package's own generator and re-bake the corpus folds (`gate:fold`, `gate:fold-ts`, `specimens-0.1.0.json`), each re-pin traced to the fence. Operator-approved 2026-09-18.

''Hazards:'' two worktrees edit one grammar file, so merge in order and re-run every gate after each merge · the parent tree carries another writer's open work, so every commit stays `git commit --only`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hazards>>

! Standing hazards on the shared tree

* ''Operator boot-seed edits ride dirty'' — `noosphere-boot.mem` · `ai-phrasebook.mem` are the operator's own live edits; NO hand touches, stamps, or commits them. Every commit stays `git commit --only -- <paths>`.
* ''The e2e set flakes at file level'' (`minted-canon-projection`, `smoke`, `herm-floor` have each flipped) — run-twice, never trust one pass; never run two e2e sets at once (shared `synced-tree.json`).
* ''Wall-clock residue beyond the ring — `:225` GROUNDED (2026-09-18 scout)'' — `:814` + `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:130` CLEARED (`6b0910fbc`, epoch-lease licensed). `daemon-auth-gate.ts:225` (`contractNymOf(edge, ident, Date.now())`) now READ: it GATES (a real `now > expires+drift` reject inside `verifyDeviceDelegation` at `device-delegation.ts:173`), but the code documents it as job-(c) — a REPLAY BACKSTOP over a long-lived revocable grant, NOT the "still-authorized" decision (that rides the CRDT membership graph + `boundEpoch` lease). A failure only OMITS the `contractNym` (peer stands at the cross-operator floor); the WS admission is the worker's V3 verdict, decided before `:225` runs. ''Clean-as-designed, NOT a violation.'' The HandleCard half of the old flag is VOID — `daemon-auth-gate.ts` never touches `HandleCard` (that's a distinct self-documented local-clock lease in `lararium-mesh/src/handle-card.ts:236`, off this line). ''One residual thread (not a violation, a completeness gap):'' `:225` passes NO `expectedEpoch`, so the clockless lease branch (`device-delegation.ts:182`) never runs at THIS call site — the wall-clock is the ONLY freshness check for the CONTRACT slot here. `nexus-carriage.ts:29-37` calls this deliberate ("no lease here — the contract names the RELATION"), but no integration test covers an expired `contractEdge` at the gate. If ever pursued: an expiry test in `daemon-auth-gate.test.ts` + a one-line cross-ref comment at `:225` so a future reader doesn't re-flag it. `daemon-auth-gate.ts` is UNHELD/open ground. (`recovery-keel`'s readmit epoch is LANDED — `592f46d0d`; the oracle-pointer clocks stay tracked in `no-global-now.mem`.)
* ''The R0 / REGION coordination seam'' — the Codex crew holds R0's DESIGN (their B6/C2) but R0's reds live in `open-node-vessel.ts` (founding boot ground); whichever hearth builds it CROSSES — name the crossing before a hand starts.
* ''CLOSED — the `two-vessel-mesh.test.ts` red'' — was two causes (Vessel B's identity leak + Vessel A founding faceless); both fixed (`e06d2ddda` + `b9c0f591a`), 11/11 green. FO3's compile-gate is now CI-backed by a runtime arity assertion (`46aaeb698`) — a regression reds under plain vitest.
* ''Browser-leaf behavioral proof owed — GROUNDED (2026-09-18 scout)'' — a REAL-Chromium harness DOES exist (`tools/browser-weld/leaf-continuity.mjs`, playwright `chromium.launchPersistentContext` against a live Vite server), but it drives ONLY the ③ anchor-scope climb (offline-found → `?gate=<ANCHOR>` → reload; C4.1-C4.5), NEVER the admit/join-a-PersonaGroup path. The `admit` branch of `openBrowserVessel` (`packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts:450-458` → `admittedJoineeIsland`; `:503-534` seeds the joinee's slot from `CarriedAdmitPayload`, never derived locally) has coverage ONLY at the pure-function/decode level (`admit-carriage.test.ts` round-trips `parseAdmitCarriage`, no boot) plus a source-text fault-pin (`nexus-board-climb-at-leaf.test.ts` — its own docstring admits `openBrowserVessel` "cannot stand in a unit test"). ''Real debt confirmed.'' A true proof needs a sibling to `leaf-continuity.mjs`: found a founder in Chromium profile A, mint a real `CarriedAdmitPayload` off its root+edge, carry it via `admit-carriage.ts` into fresh profile B, boot `openBrowserVessel({ admit })`, assert the joinee's `nexusPubkey`/board matches the founder's island (the exact ③ Option-A defect class). ''Ground note:'' `tools/browser-weld/*` is Codex-Lares-held LIVE (`hearths.mem`, trailer `…a0a6f209…`) — building the proof CROSSES into Codex ground, needs a handoff crossing row, not a unilateral add. (The source files it touches — `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `nexus-identity.ts`, `keyhive/index.ts` — are unheld/open.)
* ''`dist/` is STALE against ③ + ⑤ + native-parity source'' (2026-09-18) — run `pnpm -r build` (mesh→tw5→node) before any e2e or live daemon boot; do NOT rebuild while an e2e runs (shared dist). (The e2e spirit rebuilds the chain as part of its red/green cycle.)
* ''Two small follow-ons surfaced, both `more-work-now` candidates'' — (a) `recovery-keel.ts`'s `runReadmitEdge` (a 4th caller of `runDeviceAdmitEdge`) still mints `boundEpoch ?? 0`, so a recovery-readmitted device reads maximally stale if the group rolled since founding — the consistent completion of `:814` (backward-compatible today). (b) `identityDir()` in `node-vessel-identity.ts` IGNORES its `dataDir` param (reads `LAR_ROOT`/XDG only) — an isolation footgun a caller passing a dir would be bitten by.

<<~/ahu>>

